#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "CAP-IDENTITY Identity and groups"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "One identity provider for people and groups, synchronised automatically, with break-glass access held apart."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: governance"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "The organisation's identity provider is the one source of people and groups."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Users and groups created locally drift away from the organisation's real ones. Group renames don't propagate reliably, so group names are fixed once they're created."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Automatic provisioning of users and groups into every service, for example with SCIM."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Group declarations in the platform repository."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Two break-glass accounts."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "A change of membership can take minutes to show up in a browser, and longer in jobs. Most clouds also have indirect ways to become an administrator, so list them."
msgstr ""

