#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "CAP-IDENTITY.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "The organisation's identity provider is the only source of users, groups and membership, synchronised to every platform service automatically."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "No platform service has a locally created user or group except break-glass accounts."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "CAP-IDENTITY.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Group names are frozen once created, because renames do not propagate reliably."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "The group declarations forbid renames (a rename is a new group plus migration)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "CAP-IDENTITY.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Two break-glass accounts exist, outside the identity provider's normal sign-in, protected by hardware keys, monitored on every use."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Sign-in by either account raises an alert."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "CAP-IDENTITY.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Indirect administrator paths (a directory role that becomes a platform administrator, a resource role that grants workspace administration) are closed or monitored."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "The access review lists each such path and its control."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "CAP-IDENTITY.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Administrators and every role that can read identifiable or special-category data (T3, T4) authenticate at NIST SP 800-63-4 authentication assurance level 2 or higher with a phishing-resistant authenticator, such as a WebAuthn passkey; platform administrators and holders of the root of trust authenticate at level 3.{1}*Example:* A support officer who can read special-category records signs in with a passkey; a password with a text-message code is refused for that role."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Sign-in policy for those roles requires it; a sign-in without it is refused."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "CAP-IDENTITY.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "Learners, guardians and members of the public authenticate through a separate external identity tenant or portal, and are never members of platform groups."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-identity.md
msgid "No platform group contains an external identity."
msgstr ""

